      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.mtjade1_factory_network", decl_name: "srv13_bmc_observed_network"),
    ],
  },
  question: "Which slot is the ALTRAD8UD-1L2T with board serial BR80S6102300049, and how do the machine-intake witnesses keep replaying its 2026-10-07 captures at 192.168.1.247 once srv13 stops being a fleet host?",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: srv13_srv15_sighting_revision,
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesArtifact {
          label: "artifacts/bmc/srv13-first-contact-2026-10-07/bmc-3.22.00/root_Systems_system.json (SerialNumber BR80S6102300049)",
          sha256: Sha256Digest { hex: "fd4ad69ffdbef8db4e21eedb4b7c107627abd662d9f0bc3fd0effff1484469da" as Sha256DigestHex },
        },
        tail: [
          CitesArtifact {
            label: "artifacts/bmc/srv15-inband-recovery-2026-10-29/redfish_v1_Systems_system.json (SerialNumber BR80S6102300049)",
            sha256: Sha256Digest { hex: "281dbfefd5d55d5c30b2d6f730d45d28062162bc9a2d5ce6be396a30bbfe948a" as Sha256DigestHex },
          },
          CitesArtifact {
            label: "artifacts/bmc/srv13-first-contact-2026-10-07/FINDINGS.txt (BMC 192.168.1.247 MAC 9c:6b:00:e7:c9:83; host NIC 9C:6B:00:E7:CA:63)",
            sha256: Sha256Digest { hex: "81bb5b9576a26c909ed769ebb3ae75cc85c3397192ec82e2a98613e329041567" as Sha256DigestHex },
          },
          CitesArtifact {
            label: "artifacts/bmc/srv15-inband-recovery-2026-10-29/00_README.txt (BMC 192.168.1.248 MAC 9c:6b:00:e7:c9:e7; board serial BR80S6102300049; host lease from NIC 9c:6b:00:e7:ca:63)",
            sha256: Sha256Digest { hex: "6f4a3c900238b2575d386bd4b6d96cb014e1d8439d3b2274b988d8644b8e0d4e" as Sha256DigestHex },
          },
        ],
      },
      account: "Both slots' captures report board serial BR80S6102300049 and host NIC 9c:6b:00:e7:ca:63, an Intel I210 address burned into the board; only the controller's MAC and lease differ, across a BMC firmware push from 2.07.00 to 3.22.00 that srv13's own capture records. Read-only on 2026-11-05: the controller at .248 serves Redfish with srv13's captured ServiceEntryPointUUID, and the router shows srv13's reservation (.247) inactive. srv15's recovery also found the root credential changed by hand without a record, which is what srv13's forced first rotation would leave. Not established: whether the MAC change came from the firmware push or from a later reflash.",
    },
    tail: [],
  },
  // CLOSED (smart-crane-730, 2026-11-10; the operator retired srv13 and keeps srv15, "bobo"). The captures
  // keep their provenance: they replay against the endpoint their own network observation names
  // (gunbc.machine_intake.mtjade1_factory_network srv13_bmc_observed_network, 192.168.1.247), reached through
  // gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_rotation_route_evidence observed_bmc_network_endpoint, so no row claims a
  // controller the board no longer has. Both preserved obligations stay executed by their controls below.
  disposition: Integrated { evidence: IntegrationEvidence {
    integrated_at: "7bbb4efaebd8eda775478d65c6ac74692367028b" as CommitSha,
    superseded: [
      HistoricalDeclaration { at: "495211eb3196d6c3e11b7322cf5900f375dce07e" as CommitSha, module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_identity", decl_name: "operator_host_srv13" },
      HistoricalDeclaration { at: "495211eb3196d6c3e11b7322cf5900f375dce07e" as CommitSha, module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent", decl_name: "srv13_baseboard" },
      HistoricalDeclaration { at: "495211eb3196d6c3e11b7322cf5900f375dce07e" as CommitSha, module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_write_controller", decl_name: "srv13_bmc_write_controller" },
      HistoricalDeclaration { at: "495211eb3196d6c3e11b7322cf5900f375dce07e" as CommitSha, module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_rotation_route_evidence", decl_name: "mtjade1_observed_endpoint" },
    ],
    replacement: FreeSemigroup {
      head: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_identity", decl_name: "operator_host_srv15"),
      tail: [
        decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_write_controller", decl_name: "srv15_bmc_write_controller"),
        decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_rotation_route_evidence", decl_name: "observed_bmc_network_endpoint"),
        decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_credential_policy_witness", decl_name: "first_contact_capture_controller"),
      ],
    },
    executions: FreeSemigroup {
      head: RetainedExecutionResult {
        control: decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_write_controller_witness", decl_name: "srv15_admits_a_per_write_approval_at_its_own_controller"),
        run: "claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/machine_intake/machine_intake_bmc_write_controller_witness.dag (every test fn), local, at b436f77",
        conclusion: "all claims PASS; srv15's row admits a per-write approval only at its current controller and refuses the controller the board had at first contact as another endpoint",
      },
      tail: [
        RetainedExecutionResult {
          control: decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_forced_first_rotation_witness", decl_name: "the_forced_state_admits_only_its_own_controller_and_build"),
          run: "claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/machine_intake/machine_intake_bmc_forced_first_rotation_witness.dag (every test fn), local, at 7bbb4ef",
          conclusion: "10/10 PASS: the 2026-10-07 captures replay at 192.168.1.247 and still refuse another controller or build (the file did not compile at 495211e without this branch's import fix)",
        },
        RetainedExecutionResult {
          control: decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.fleet_naming_witness", decl_name: "witness_binding_for_another_member_refuses"),
          run: "claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/fleet_naming_witness.dag (every test fn), local, at 7bbb4ef",
          conclusion: "37/37 PASS with srv14 standing in as the other member srv13 used to be",
        },
      ],
    },
  } },
}

data run_closure_typecheck_exceeds_eval_demand: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "run_closure_typecheck_exceeds_eval_demand",
  kind: SuspectedCapabilityGap {
    model: decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.demand_acquire", decl_name: "resolve_entry_graph_demand_acquired"),
    requirement: "a gunbc run pays memory and wall time for the part of its entry's closure that evaluation reaches, not for every module the import closure names, while every refusal that typechecking the closure raises today still fires where it fires today",
    standing: RequirementEstablished { by: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "realization_of") } },
  },
  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.demand_acquire", decl_name: "resolve_entry_graph_demand_acquired"),
    tail: [decl_ref(module_path: "v2.compiler.module_acquisition", decl_name: "acquisition_lookup")],
  },
  question: "Is the pre-entry typecheck of a gunbc run's whole demand-acquired closure owed, or is it the larger half of the private lanes' memory floor that no model has yet been asked to narrow? Measured at seed e1f753b9 with the private overlay: the private drift entry typechecks 2918 closure modules, the roster entry 3245, and evaluation touches 227-278 of them (about 9.5 percent); the isolated audit_packet_witness entry reaches 12.9 GiB at the end of pre-entry (closure_typecheck 664,822 ms over 2775 files) before evaluation starts. This floor is undesigned and carries no estimate: the whole-pool burst (keyed_module_reads_walk_the_whole_pool) is the named, repairable part, and removing it leaves this floor standing.",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: "f08a6ae4e44dc0636eda71f25f0009e97ffde1d1",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.demand_acquire", decl_name: "resolve_entry_graph_demand_acquired") },
        tail: [],
      },
      account: "Bisect of the private projection-drift regression (2026-11-05) and two isolated srv1 runs (qn-roster-peak40: roster cgroup peak 35.88 GiB; qn-auditpacket-peak40: audit_packet_witness VmHWM 26.84 GiB) put roughly 13-16 GiB of each private lane in pre-entry typecheck and the rest in one whole-pool burst plus per-witness evaluation. The same floor shows up as wall time on small entries: a read-only runner_host_file_observe on srv3 (run 42037046961) spent its whole 15-minute step typechecking v2.compiler modules its entry's closure names and timed out before reading a drop-in. Recorded so a lane blocked on it can cite a named cause rather than an assertion; no fix is designed.",
    },
    tail: [ConcernSighting {
      revision: "35812db9f22",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "realization_of") },
        tail: [CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "realization_profile_diagnostic") }],
      },
      account: "Public-corpus measurement of this floor at the fleet_converge_plan_wet acceptance entry, before the declaration-grain cut landed on this branch: compile.reconcile 11 minutes, whole run 931 s, peak RSS 16.5 GiB, with 3318 closure modules realized in full while only 796 of them held a demanded function body and the demanded declarations were 4915 of 49699 (about 10 percent). After the cut (the same entry, same machine): reconcile 9 minutes, run 776 s, peak RSS 11.0 GiB, zero realization gaps. The wall dropped less than the realized fraction because the per-module frame -- context assembly, parent merging, provider settlement over the dense closure -- is still paid for all 3318 modules; that residue is what stays open under this concern now that bodies and declarations are demanded.",
    }, ConcernSighting {
      revision: "61b01423d11",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "realization_of") },
        tail: [CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "typecheck_module_demanded") }],
      },
      account: "Per-phase profile of the 9-minute residue (a temporary instrumented run: atomic timers around the census build, the realization pass, the first-pass per-module fold and the per-module machinery inside it; counters reverted, never committed). The first-pass realize_module fold is about 450 s of the roughly 540 s reconcile, and inside it build_module_context alone is 308 s -- paid by all 3324 modules, 2309 of which carry ZERO realized declarations. The census is 11.6 s and the realization pass 3.6 s: corpus-proportional but not the floor. Cutting the empty-realization modules' frame (context, analysis, audit over no inputs; the type env still builds so their own import diagnostics keep firing) took the same entry to reconcile 4 minutes, whole run about 6 minutes, peak RSS 9.7 GiB, zero realization gaps. What still stays open under this concern: the per-module frame of the 1015 modules that DO carry realized declarations, and the census plus realization passes.",
    }],
  },
  disposition: Open,
}


data grain_witness_tests_are_hand_written_rust_in_the_stage0_mirror: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "grain_witness_tests_are_hand_written_rust_in_the_stage0_mirror",
  kind: SuspectedCapabilityGap {
    model: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "realization_of"),
    requirement: "Hand-written Rust added inside the generated stage0 mirror must carry a checkable receipt -- a deleted scaffold path, a before/after seed census, or a deferral naming a lane and a tracking row (ctrl review policy). #16156 added about 345 lines of hand-written witness Rust at src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/demanded_typecheck_equivalence.rs (the declaration-grain tests: inactive grain equals #16069, unreached stays unseen, reachable errors still refuse, out-of-set reads refuse typed, alias-body and provider-row reachability, the corpus witness). This row is the deferral: the witnesses are owed a landing -- rewritten as generated .dag test sources under the corpus, or admitted as a standing hand-written exception with a file-level receipt -- and the lane that decides and executes it is follow-up node adhoc-0eedbb6e-a35, the same node named by gunbc.design_ruling::run_realizes_only_demanded_declarations for enrolling the by-hand demanded_scope controls.",
    standing: RequirementEstablished {
      by: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_ruling", decl_name: "run_realizes_only_demanded_declarations") },
    },
  },
  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "realization_of"),
    tail: [decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "typecheck_module_demanded")],
  },
  question: "Where do the hand-written grain witnesses end up? They test the declaration-grain realization from the host side and today live as hand-written Rust beside generated code in the stage0 mirror. The deferral names lane node adhoc-0eedbb6e-a35 and this tracking row: at enrollment the node either moves the witnesses into generated .dag test sources or records them as a standing hand-written exception with a receipt comment at the file, so no hand-written block in the mirror remains unaccounted.",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: "5a0a692fa9b",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "realization_of") },
        tail: [CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "typecheck_module_demanded") }],
      },
      account: "Raised by review artifact 92786 on PR #16156: the PR adds src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/demanded_typecheck_equivalence.rs (~345 lines of hand-written Rust) next to the generated mirror; the ruling's enrollment deferral covered the demanded_scope controls but named no landing for these witnesses. This row is that landing plan; the witnesses currently run green in the release profile on the head they test.",
    },
    tail: [],
  },
  disposition: Open,
}
