data equality_synthesis_helper_binding_is_import_authority: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "equality_synthesis_helper_binding_is_import_authority",
  kind: SuspectedCapabilityGap {
    model: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "equality_synth_qcall"),
    requirement: "a generated comparison body binds the equality vocabulary it calls (std.algebra map_values_eq / zip_eq, std.optional optional_eq, and the routed equality functions) by the declaring identity of the named declaration, independent of the holder module's import set, as the derived equality already binds `==` by the type's own declaration",
    standing: RequirementEstablished { by: CitesArtifact { label: "new-interpreter compile of a pre-#15175 dag tree: 49 hard 'function std.algebra.map_values_eq not found in scope (<derived:v2.std.symbol_index>)' -- resolution of the synthesized body tracked the holder's selective imports", sha256: Sha256Digest { hex: "88c2cf1e3de156a200f8bf5fefdb03e075de3ab7577e8b0b4c8b3d6c89e9d6c2" as Sha256DigestHex } } },
  },
  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "equality_synth_qcall"),
    tail: [
      decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "equality_synthesized_for"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "std.algebra", decl_name: "map_values_eq"),
    ],
  },
  question: "Should synthesized equality calls carry a resolved declaring reference (like the derived equality's own == binding) instead of a name spelling resolved through the holder's imports? Trigger: synthesized equality binds helpers by declaring identity. (#15972's interim gate equality_helpers_visible and its import-enumeration interim were reverted by #16000 on operator decision; they re-land with #15992 and this row's sightings then resume.)",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: "3bb5cbff9dad86fec9636a6f5ba82a675b504e66",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.std.symbol_index", decl_name: "SymbolIndex") },
        tail: [CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "equality_synth_compare") }],
      },
      account: "symbol_index imports std.algebra without map_values_eq while v2.std.node imports zip_eq; the same synthesized-body mechanism resolves in one holder and dangles in the other, so the import set -- not the equality model -- decides. Observed as 49 hard diagnostics under a new interpreter over a dag tree predating #15175's import co-update.",
    },
    tail: [ConcernSighting {
      revision: "3bb5cbff9dad86fec9636a6f5ba82a675b504e66",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesArtifact { label: "main-tree host_effect closure compile with the #15175 interpreter: 1 blocking diagnostic (CreateCause), derived bodies clean -- green only because every holder imports what the emitter spells", sha256: Sha256Digest { hex: "7cc9e9d96b7c0c51734e99422f98fcdefbc04e2f425cf22cc3a8f8f1b777e71c" as Sha256DigestHex } },
        tail: [],
      },
      account: "On main's own tree the family is latent, not broken: the co-updated imports carry every spelled name, so the import-as-authority defect shows only when emitter and imports drift (mixed-tree compile above) or a new holder forgets a name.",
    }],
  },
  disposition: Open,
}

data entry_closure_provider_settling_has_two_loops: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "entry_closure_provider_settling_has_two_loops",
  kind: SuspectedFork {
    authorities: DistinctAuthorities {
      first: decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.demand_acquire", decl_name: "demand_acquired_provider_fixed_point"),
      second: decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.provider_acquire", decl_name: "compile_to_provider_fixed_point_with"),
      rest: [],
    },
  },
  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.demand_acquire", decl_name: "demand_acquired_entry_resolved"),
    tail: [decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.entry_resolve", decl_name: "resolve_entry_typed")],
  },
  question: "Two loops answer one question, how an entry closure is settled once generated providers join it: gunbc run rebuilds the acquired index with seeds and resolves through the lossy resolve_entry_typed (empty OccurrenceTransport), while the entry compile runs a complete .dag compile per provider round over a growing source list. Is the run loop to migrate onto the .dag resolution (semantic home std.occurrence_identity and compile.dag), or does gunbc run owe something the compile loop cannot give? Migrating run is out of scope of the change that made the compile loop the single resolution for emission.",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: "465d3d96ba6a92138f61beef36421225ffc456b6",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.demand_acquire", decl_name: "demand_acquired_provider_fixed_point") },
        tail: [CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.provider_acquire", decl_name: "compile_to_provider_fixed_point_with") }],
      },
      account: "Found while carrying the acquired resolution into the entry compile (gunbc#16018): the entry compile now settles through compile_to_provider_fixed_point_with, and gunbc run keeps its own loop over resolve_entry_typed.",
    },
    tail: [],
  },
  disposition: Integrated { evidence: IntegrationEvidence {
    integrated_at: "659366e59a0cbb0aa4e43edd99194cc03a0fd435" as CommitSha,
    // Declarations removed at the integrated revision, cited at the last revision where each existed
    // (1bdf7152): demand_acquired_provider_fixed_point was the lossy provider-settling loop (resolve
    // through an empty OccurrenceTransport); the 3-tuple _with_diagnostics wrapper had no consumer (its
    // 'serve' doc was stale: serving is an admitted result of gunbc run, not a separate command);
    // resolve_entry_typed lost its last consumer when that loop went.
    superseded: [
      HistoricalDeclaration { at: "1bdf7152f7259c7475995d937542524f4a822358" as CommitSha, module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.demand_acquire", decl_name: "demand_acquired_provider_fixed_point" },
      HistoricalDeclaration { at: "1bdf7152f7259c7475995d937542524f4a822358" as CommitSha, module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.demand_acquire", decl_name: "resolve_entry_graph_demand_acquired_with_diagnostics" },
      HistoricalDeclaration { at: "1bdf7152f7259c7475995d937542524f4a822358" as CommitSha, module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.entry_resolve", decl_name: "resolve_entry_typed" },
    ],
    // ONE loop answers the question: run/ingress/orchestrator settle through the surviving
    // demand-acquired wrapper -> demand_acquired_entry_resolved -> compile_to_provider_fixed_point_with
    // (the entry compile's authority since #16018), consuming its settled graph.
    replacement: FreeSemigroup { head: decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.demand_acquire", decl_name: "resolve_entry_graph_demand_acquired"), tail: [decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.demand_acquire", decl_name: "demand_acquired_entry_resolved")] },
    executions: FreeSemigroup { head: RetainedExecutionResult { control: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge", decl_name: "runner_host_file_converge_ci_wet"), run: "gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/gunbc/runner/runner_host_file_converge.dag --function __no_such_function__ (resolve-only; baseline 1bdf7152 sha256 acd2d803 vs migrated 659366e5 sha256 b31ebf1b)", conclusion: "behavior byte-identical: refuses the same 3 interpreter-blocking equality-admission diags with byte-identical 'resolve failed' text; resolve_entry_graph_inclusive 1,387,455 -> 1,432,729 ms (+45 s within jitter), max_rss 15.44 -> 16.26 GiB; closure_ownership stays 0 ms (the run-settle skip works)" }, tail: [RetainedExecutionResult { control: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_plan_cli", decl_name: "fleet_converge_plan_wet"), run: "gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/gunbc/fleet/fleet_converge_plan_cli.dag --function __no_such_function__ (resolve-only; 3174 modules)", conclusion: "baseline 1bdf7152 resolve_entry_graph_inclusive 1,492,830 ms max_rss 16.24 GiB; migrated same equality-admission refusal text, no wall regression" }] },
  } },
}

// srv1 #15822 row 29 (#16013): the pre-launch memory-fit admission refuses a review that cannot fit the
// user-work slice, returning ReviewDeferred rather than launching a unit the kernel would memcg-OOM. A
// deferral is cheap (retries each tick) but, by design, has no expiry -- so a slice that never drains
// wedges the review with no signal that it is stuck. This row records that missing signal.
data user_work_slice_admission_deferral_has_no_visible_count: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "user_work_slice_admission_deferral_has_no_visible_count",
  kind: SuspectedCapabilityGap {
    model: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_review_spawn"),
    requirement: "A review or audit that the user-work-slice memory-fit admission keeps deferring must expose a cumulative, visible refusal count. A deferral retries each tick and never expires, so a slice that cannot drain wedges the review with no signal distinguishing 'briefly full' from 'permanently full'. The per-deferral reason carries the requested/available byte counts, but nothing counts deferrals across ticks.",
    standing: RequirementEstablished {
      by: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_audit_spawn") },
    },
  },
  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_review_spawn"),
    tail: [decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_audit_spawn")],
  },
  question: "Where is a chronically-deferred review made visible? belt_review_spawn and belt_audit_spawn now refuse before launch (typed memory-fit admission, #16013) when gunbc-user-work.slice cannot hold the work. Each refusal carries its byte counts in the ReviewDeferred.reason, but a single reason per tick does not reveal that the same review has been refused for hundreds of ticks while the standing obligation daemons keep the slice full. A cumulative count must live where the belt already records per-tick outcomes (a tick outcome record/journal) -- not in the attempt record, which must not carry a belt-lifecycle fact it does not own (the row-30 boundary, confirmed with the row-30 owner).",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: "50652e0777329a585efa6919ef5ab9a0c81222ae",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_review_spawn") },
        tail: [CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_audit_spawn") }],
      },
      account: "Raised while repairing srv1 #15822 row 29 (#16013): the goal-audit reviewer was memcg-OOM-killed because the belt admitted it into gunbc-user-work.slice on slot count and liveness alone. The repair adds a pre-launch memory-fit admission that returns ReviewDeferred when the slice cannot hold the unit. The row-30 owner noted that a deferral holds forever by design (no expiry) and asked that the refusal count be surfaced somewhere visible; the belt spawn is per-tick and holds no cross-tick store, and the deferral never reaches the reconciliation standings fold, so neither the belt nor the attempt record persists a count today. This row records that gap rather than inventing cross-tick state in #16013.",
    },
    tail: [],
  },
  disposition: Open,
}

data user_work_slice_admission_check_races_within_a_tick: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "user_work_slice_admission_check_races_within_a_tick",
  kind: SuspectedCapabilityGap {
    model: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_user_work_slice_fit"),
    requirement: "A pre-launch memory-fit admission must account for units already admitted in the same tick, so two spawns cannot both pass a fit check against the same free room. belt_user_work_slice_fit reads the slice MemoryCurrent and the belt then launches separately; the read and the launch are not one atomic step, so simultaneous admissions may jointly overcommit the ceiling before the kernel's accounting reflects either launch.",
    standing: RequirementEstablished {
      by: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_audit_spawn") },
    },
  },
  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_user_work_slice_fit"),
    tail: [decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_review_spawn"), decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_audit_spawn")],
  },
  question: "When several reviewers or auditors are admitted in one belt tick, what prevents them from each passing belt_user_work_slice_fit against the same slice MemoryCurrent reading before any of their launches is reflected in the kernel's accounting? A per-tick reservation -- subtracting the bounded bytes of units already admitted this tick from the free room before each subsequent fit check -- would close the window. The check already removes the dominant failure (launching into an already-full slice); this row records the residual within-a-tick window rather than claiming it closed.",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: "50652e0777329a585efa6919ef5ab9a0c81222ae",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_user_work_slice_fit") },
        tail: [CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_review_spawn") }, CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_audit_spawn") }],
      },
      account: "Raised on the #16013 review of the srv1 #15822 row-29 repair: the pre-launch memory-fit admission reads the slice and then launches as separate steps, so two spawns admitted in one tick can both observe enough free room. A per-tick reservation of already-admitted bounded bytes would make the check exact. The check still prevents the incident (launching a reviewer into a slice the standing daemons already fill); this row records the remaining race, not a defect in the incident repair.",
    },
    tail: [],
  },
  disposition: Open,
}

// RAISED BY WORK ITEM adhoc-d9a8b550-3f7 (2026-11-07), from a regen round observed 2026-11-06 06:18Z.
// The round printed git's refusal to resolve a bare `main` and CONTINUED to exit 0. Nothing here was
// built or executed: the trace is source reading plus one read-only scratch repo used to match git's
// error strings, and the round-time binary and head object are both gone.
data base_mirror_round_sighting_revision: CommitSha = "700fe5008e3826a82105ae081d449f7c4ac5966d"

data base_mirror_round_tolerates_unresolvable_base_git_failure: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "base_mirror_round_tolerates_unresolvable_base_git_failure",

  kind: SuspectedCapabilityGap {
    model: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_diff_observe", decl_name: "floor_base_ref_verdict"),
    requirement: "an observation that asks git whether a base ref resolves must yield an outcome its caller cannot drop: a fatal printed on stderr while the round continues and exits 0 is not an outcome, and gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed requires a failure arm to refuse rather than widen",
    standing: RequirementUnestablished { decided_by: "identify, in a build pinned to main, the caller that handed a bare `main` to a git operation during `claim_executor --regen-round-cost --base-mirror`; if no such caller exists on main the requirement is not established here and this row closes as branch-side" },
  },

  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_diff_observe", decl_name: "floor_base_ref_verdict"),
    tail: [
      decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_diff_observe", decl_name: "floor_run_git_diff_unified"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.diff_baseline", decl_name: "resolve_diff_baseline"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.diff_baseline", decl_name: "resolve_merge_target"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.regen_candidate_reverts_hand_authored_mirror", decl_name: "regen_candidate_reverts_hand_authored_mirror"),
    ],
  },

  question: "When git cannot resolve the base a round is about to diff against, is there any model-level outcome that stops the round — or can a caller print git's fatal, ignore it, and reach exit 0 with the tree rewritten?",

  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: base_mirror_round_sighting_revision,
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_diff_observe", decl_name: "floor_base_ref_verdict") },
        tail: [
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.diff_baseline", decl_name: "resolve_diff_baseline") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.diff_baseline", decl_name: "resolve_merge_target") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.merge_admission_subject", decl_name: "merge_admission_merge_base_ref") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.git", decl_name: "Diff") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.git", decl_name: "DiffNameOnly") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.git", decl_name: "DiffNameOnlyNoRenames") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.git", decl_name: "DiffNameOnlyMerge") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.git.inspect", decl_name: "ResolveRefCommit") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.cross_pr_contradiction_instrument", decl_name: "observe_pull_request") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.merge_admission_capture", decl_name: "tested_subject_capture") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.merge_admission_current_context", decl_name: "main") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.merge_admission_walk", decl_name: "merge_target_refresh") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.path_writer_set_instrument", decl_name: "observe_pull_request") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.pr_containment_instrument", decl_name: "establish_containment_subject") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.pr_containment_instrument", decl_name: "classify_branch") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.namespace_cut.namespace_step0_subject_collector", decl_name: "collect_step0_subject_vector_at") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.regen_candidate_reverts_hand_authored_mirror", decl_name: "regen_candidate_reverts_hand_authored_mirror") },
        ],
      },
      account: "A `--base-mirror` regen round (`claim_executor --regen-round-cost --base-mirror`, base supplied bare as HEAL_BASE_MIRROR_COMMIT) run in a clone with neither refs/heads/main nor refs/remotes/origin/main printed, mid-round: `fatal: ambiguous argument 'main': unknown revision or path not in the working tree. Use '--' to separate paths from revisions`, then the floor teardown line, then exit 0 with 11 modified files under src/v1/stage0/. git's exit code was 128 and the round did not stop. WHICH CALLER IS UNKNOWN. The exact string is produced by `git show -s --format=%H main`, `git diff main HEAD` and `git diff --name-only main HEAD` (each run against a scratch repo to compare strings), and NOT by the changed-mirror scope operation — its argv renders `main...HEAD` as one argument — and NOT by the round's worktree-versus-index observation, which takes no revision at all and prints `fatal: bad revision 'main'`. So the failure came from a `git.Inspect.ResolveRefCommit`-shaped or `extdeps.git` diff-shaped operation given a bare branch name. THE CANDIDATE CALLERS, each named by its enclosing declaration with the position beside it: `observe_pull_request` (gunbc.instruments.cross_pr_contradiction_instrument:219), `tested_subject_capture` (gunbc.instruments.merge_admission_capture:168), `main` (gunbc.instruments.merge_admission_current_context:121), `merge_target_refresh` (gunbc.instruments.merge_admission_walk:334), `observe_pull_request` (gunbc.instruments.path_writer_set_instrument:230), `establish_containment_subject` and `classify_branch` (gunbc.instruments.pr_containment_instrument:237 and :511), and `collect_step0_subject_vector_at` (gunbc.namespace_cut.namespace_step0_subject_collector:392); on the operation side `Diff`, `DiffNameOnly`, `DiffNameOnlyNoRenames` and `DiffNameOnlyMerge` (dag/extdeps/git.dag:1830, :1842, :1857 and :1873), whose `head` input defaults to `HEAD`. No data-row base on main is bare: `merge_admission_merge_base_ref` (gunbc.merge_admission_subject:76) is `gunbc_merge_target_ref`, origin/main, and `resolve_merge_target` (gunbc.diff_baseline:233-:245, called from `resolve_diff_baseline`) composes `origin/<name>` for a merge target, while gunbc.extdeps.git's `default_branch_names` has no consumers. THE UNKNOWN STATED PLAINLY: the round ran from a branch-tree build at 6f4cfe70d792 whose round-time head cca9623369be is pruned, so a branch-side caller that resolved `main` directly cannot be excluded — which is why this stands as a concern with an unestablished requirement rather than as a defect with a site.",
    },
    tail: [],
  },

  disposition: Open,
}

// ── CREDENTIAL CONSOLIDATION, P1 (shared RFC 3339 instant; credential validity) ──────────────────
